<title>SWEDEN: Trygg-Hansa posts 31 pct rise '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Trygg-Hansa posts 31 pct rise '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Trygg-Hansa AB results for the 12 months to December 1, 1996. The comparison figures for 1995 do not include recent aquisitions Trygg-Banken, Fri Placering and Trygg Fonder apart from premium income which shows total operations.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    2,425 vs  1,847</p>
<p>   Non-life infe insurance		 750 vs    577</p>
<p>   Other operations			1,675 vs  1,270</p>
<p> Proposed dividend/shr (SKR)	    2.50 vs   2.00</p>
<p> Result/shr after tax (SKR)	    28.50 vs  19.10</p>
<p> Gross premiums written		 12,100 vs 11,777</p>
<p>   Non-life insurance		    5,895 vs  6,465</p>
<p>   Life insurance (index-linked)	 920 vs    649</p>
<p>   Commissioned operations	     5,285 vs  4,663</p>
<p> Deposits with Trygg-Hansa	     1,529 vs    101</p>
<p> Trygg Fonder, managed assets	  5,659 vs  3,574</p>
<p> Adjusted shhldrs equity/shr (SKR)     112 vs     83</p>
<p> Equity ratio (pct)			   28 vs     24</p>
<p> Solvency Margin (pct)		     188 vs    130</p>
<p> Combined ratio, net (pct)		 107 vs    110</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll forecast Trygg-Hansa would post a pre-tax profit of 2.61 billion crowns for calendar 1996. Any comparison with 1995 profits was not relevant due to changes in accountancy rules.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
